Today we are reading Matthew chapter 11 verses 1-6 from the ESV bible translation



Jesus just finished instructing his disciples about their mission to go out two by two to preach the gospel

Jesus then responds to a message from John sent by Johns disciples where John questions and doubts whether Jesus is the Messiah



Three things I want to double click on here

1) Even John has moments of doubt or discouragement in his faith

Even the cousin of Jesus, who prepared the way for him and witnessed God say "this is my son, whom I am well pleased" when he Baptized Jesus

Mind you, John is in prison and might be frustrated and confused based on his expectations of what it would be like when Jesus arrived


  2) The second thing to double click on is that Jesus replies by descibing things that are happening which 700 years prior were predicted to happen by Isaiah

The Bible is such an incredible book


  Jesus says the blind receive sight (Isaiah 29:18)

  The lame walk (Isaiah 35:6)

The deaf hear (Isaiah 29:18)

  The dead are raised up (Isaiah 26:19)

  The good news is preached to the poor (Isaiah 61:1)

Jesus gives John plenty of proof of who He was and that rhe time of salvation prophesied by Isaiah had come.



3 - In verse 6 Jesus says:

  Blessed is the one who is not offended by me

  Blessed is actually the greek word Makarios which means highly favoured 

  Offended is actually the greek word scandalizo which means to stumble 


   "Blessed is anyone who does not stumble [take offense] on account of me" (referring to people rejecting Jesus because He didn't fit their expectations)

  Jesus warns that true blessing (makarios) belongs to those who do not lose faith or reject Him just because His methods, timing, or kingdom do not match human expectations





My take away from these 6 verses:

We all get discouraged sometimes, even John did

Don't stumble and get upset when God's timing doesnt match my desires or expectations

Instead of focusing on what isn't going well or happening as I want it to, focus on all the awesome things that God is doing for me in my life

Good reminder to avoid fixating on our plan and to trust Gods plan





